From: v0id <tyler@slaughter.pro>
Subject: render: bump ShaderProgram path to GLSL ES 3.00 (#version 300 es)

Niri hardcodes #version 100 for custom window shaders (open/close/resize),
border, and shadow — linked with texture.vert. ES 1.00 limits array
constructors and uses deprecated varying/gl_FragColor/texture2D.

This patch moves the ShaderProgram compile path to GLSL ES 3.00:
- shader_element.rs prepends #version 300 es
- texture.vert: in/out instead of attribute/varying
- Fragment preludes: in niri_v_coords, out niri_fragColor
- Epilogues + border/shadow: niri_fragColor instead of gl_FragColor
- Default resize.frag: texture() instead of texture2D()
- Custom window shaders (open/close/resize): skip DEBUG_FLAGS variant compile
  to halve driver peak memory during startup (embedded 512M MemoryMax)
- Custom window shaders: stage sources at init, compile on first animation use
- Log custom shader compile duration at info level

Smithay compile_custom_texture_shader paths (clipped_surface, gradient_fade)
and BlurProgram (blur.vert/down/up) remain ES 1.00 — separate link units.
